### Similar AI Agent Frameworks

Based on current developments in AI agent technology as of late 2025, here are several frameworks that share similarities with your Leopardess Consulting agent framework. These emphasize hierarchical or graph-based structures for organizing agents, support for heterogeneous models (e.g., different LLMs or AI/non-AI components per agent), and capabilities for tackling multifaceted, complex problems like business automation or decision-making. I've selected eight standout examples, drawing from leading options in multi-agent systems. For each, I've included a brief overview, key features, and why it's similar.

| Framework | Overview | Key Features | Similarity to Leopardess |
|-----------|----------|--------------|--------------------------|
| LangGraph | An open-source library from the LangChain ecosystem for building stateful, multi-actor AI applications. | Supports cyclical graphs with nodes and edges for workflows; stateful orchestration; integration with various tools and models. | High similarity in graph-based structures for agent coordination and ability to use different LLMs/models per node/agent, ideal for complex, multifaceted tasks. |
| CrewAI | Open-source Python framework for multi-agent AI systems where agents collaborate on tasks with assigned roles. | Role-based architecture; sequential and hierarchical task execution; real-time communication; optional LangChain integration for tools/models. | Mirrors hierarchical organization of agents and support for diverse models/capabilities, helping businesses manage AI-driven challenges through collaborative problem-solving. |
| Microsoft AutoGen | Framework for enabling multi-agent conversations to solve tasks, with customizable agents incorporating LLMs, tools, and human input. | Asynchronous messaging; heterogeneous agents with varied roles and models; supports autonomous or human-in-the-loop workflows. | Similar in allowing different AI models per agent and graph-like message passing for hierarchical interactions, suited for multifaceted problems requiring collaboration. |
| AgentOrchestra | Hierarchical multi-agent framework for general-purpose task solving, focusing on high-level planning and modular components. | Tree-like hierarchy with leader agents for planning; multimodal and generalization support; integrates diverse agents for subtasks. | Strong match with hierarchical graph structures and potential for different models per agent layer, addressing complex, adaptive business scenarios. |
| MetaGPT | Framework that simulates software engineering teams with specialized agent roles for planning, coding, and review. | Hierarchical workflows mimicking human teams (e.g., product manager to developer); task decomposition and collaboration. | Aligns with hierarchical agent structures for multifaceted problems, allowing specialized agents that could incorporate varied AI models for role-specific tasks. |
| OpenAI Swarm | Lightweight, experimental framework for multi-agent orchestration using agents and handoffs for coordination. | Simple handoff patterns for agent routing; stateless but scalable for educational/experimental use. | Moderate similarity in multi-agent setups that can imply hierarchies via handoffs, with flexibility for different models in orchestration for business problem-solving. |
| AgentFlow | Platform for multi-agent systems, often wrapping other libraries like LangChain, with a low-code interface. | Supports hierarchical and long-running agents; graph workflow sketching; secure integrations for data connectors. | Comparable graph-based and hierarchical features, enabling diverse models/tools per agent for handling AI surges in enterprise environments. |
| Hierarchical Multi-Agent Systems (HMAS) | Conceptual and operational framework for organizing AI agents in tree-like hierarchies to execute tasks efficiently. | Top-down structure with leader agents interpreting objectives; sub-agents for execution; focuses on scalability and coordination. | Direct parallel in tree/hierarchical structures for agent graphs, supporting varied models at different levels for multifaceted, real-world applications. |



